# Project Foundation

## Goals

- Single-page, scroll-driven narrative that feels modern and focused.
- Content is sourced from Astro content collections (`projects`) using MDX.
- The layout is designed to support future Static HTML Chunking (start with one chunk).

## Architecture

- Keep **layout**, **data**, and **behavior** clearly separated:
  - Layout: `BaseLayout` and section-level components (header, carousel, blog entries).
  - Data: Astro content collections and simple mapping logic.
  - Behavior: scroll orchestration and client-side enhancements in dedicated scripts.
- Treat each major section (header, carousel, blog entries) as an **independent, composable unit**:
  - Avoid cross-section DOM reach-ins; communicate via data/props, not selectors.
  - Make it easy to reorder or wrap sections without breaking behavior.

## Content Model

- Use Astro content collections with Zod schemas for all project content.
- All project data should come from MDX files in `src/content/projects/`.
- Avoid duplicating frontmatter data in components; derive UI from the collection entries.
- Prefer **typed access** (via the content collection types) whenever possible.

## Routing & Deep Linking

- The main narrative lives at `/` (single-page scroll experience).
- Dynamic routes (e.g. `/projects/[slug]`) are for **deep linking**:
  - They should resolve to the main page and scroll to the right section.
  - Each rendered project section must expose a **stable ID** based on the slug.

## Static HTML Chunking Readiness

- Start with a **single static HTML chunk** for the main page.
- Design sections so they can be split into multiple chunks later without major refactors:
  - Keep data loading at the page/layout level; pass slices down to sections.
  - Avoid tight coupling between section rendering and global scroll orchestration.
- New sections should be addable via configuration (arrays of section definitions) rather than hard-coded branching and one-off layout logic.

